Subject: HWUI: let go of an idle window's GPU caches

DSA shows each app's task in its own desktop window, and a window the user can see but does
not touch stays on screen for minutes or hours. Android trims an app's GPU caches only once its
UI is hidden (TRIM_MEMORY_UI_HIDDEN, or all its windows stopped), so a visible app that draws
nothing keeps everything its last frames left in Skia's cache: scratch textures, textures kept
by key (bitmaps, paths, shadows) and the glyph atlases, whose page is 8 MiB on a 2880x2880
display. The time-based cleanup HWUI runs after each frame lets go only of scratch resources,
and only of those the last frame did not use, and only when the render thread wakes, which an
idle window's does not. A DSA build measured 56 MiB of Vulkan memory held by the Settings app
a minute after it was last touched, of which an estimated 25 to 40 MiB could be made again.

Once the render thread has drawn no frame for 30 seconds, CacheManager now frees Skia's GPU
resources that nothing holds (GrDirectContext::freeGpuResources: unlocked scratch and keyed
resources and the atlases) and submits once more, waiting on it, so that ANGLE and Vulkan
drivers free what they deferred until they see the GPU finish the work that last used it. A
window that draws nothing submits nothing, so without that the freed memory would stay. It
logs one line each time:

  No frame for N s: let go of K KiB of GPU caches (R resources); L KiB remain

Thirty seconds is long enough that a window in use never waits for its caches again (reading,
typing pauses, a menu left open) and short enough that a window left on screen gives them back
within the minute a memory measurement waits. One release runs per quiet stretch; the next
frame uploads again what it draws (its glyphs, its bitmaps), a few milliseconds once. Surfaces,
layers and hardware bitmaps are held and stay. Nothing changes while the GPU device is lost.

Applies to frameworks/base at 45034f0663f960d9ee5fb0a101a4732b71f6e2f4 (Android 16), after 0013.
---
diff --git a/libs/hwui/renderthread/CacheManager.cpp b/libs/hwui/renderthread/CacheManager.cpp
